 "LMS_reconciliation": "The printed SI values (4.22e-9, 3.85e-9 kg/m^2) convert to sigma^(1/3) = 45.2, 43.8 keV, a factor 21.3 below the printed MeV labels; sigma differs by ~1e4 = (m/cm)^2. Reading the unit as kg/cm^2 gives sigma^(1/3) = 0.973, 0.944 MeV, within 1.5% of both labels, and gives G sigma t0 = 4.09e-06, consistent with the paper's stated agreement with the deltaT/T <~ 1e-5 estimate, whereas the literal reading gives G sigma t0 = 4.1e-10. We therefore adopt sigma_95 = 9.218e-10 GeV^3 (R+M) and 8.409e-10 GeV^3 (R+M+Lambda) as the reconciled bound and identify the MeV label with sigma^(1/3) in natural units (not a vev). This is our reconciliation, not an erratum by the authors; the literal reading is carried as a stricter alternative.",
